{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובארבע עשרה", :translit "u-v'arba esreh", :gloss "and in the fourteenth"} {:he "ב' ריש פסוק הכא", :translit "bet reish pasuk hacha", :gloss "bet beginning of verse here"} {:he "ואידך", :translit "v'idach", :gloss "and the other"} {:he "ובי״ד למלך חזקיהו עלה סנחרים", :translit "u-v'yud-dalet la-melech chirziyahu alah sancheriv", :gloss "and in the fourteenth year of King Hezekiah Sennacherib came up"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובארבע עשרה" "ובי״ד למלך חזקיהו"]}], :frame {:text "The opening bet of ובארבע עשרה (Genesis 14:5) links to the only other verse beginning with the same combination, ובי״ד למלך חזקיהו (II Kings 18:13), which recounts Sennacherib's campaign against Hezekiah. II Kings 18:13–19:37 records that Sennacherib invaded Judah in the fourteenth year of Hezekiah, and the angel of the Lord struck down 185,000 of the Assyrian camp, delivering Hezekiah from his hand. Genesis 14:1–16 records that a coalition of four kings, including the same King Chedorlaomer, made war and that Abraham pursued and defeated them, rescuing Lot. The shared opening letter thus pairs the two deliverances.", :sources ["Genesis 14:1-16" "II Kings 18:13" "II Kings 19:35"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ובארבע עשרה" "ובי״ד למלך חזקיהו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ובארבע עשרה", :refs ["Genesis 14:5" "2 Kings 18:13"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ובי״ד למלך חזקיהו", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:05:51.867911390Z", :model "glm-5.2"}